I tried to write a simplified version of rogue/nethack which would run on
an IPX/Novell Network...Unfortunately, only having 3 months I did not get
as much completed as wished for.  The main parts were completed - it was
just a case of adding in more magical items, and adjusting the rolling
stats to get a balanced game.  The multi-user part of the game, however,
worked - it was possible to simultaneously attack the same monster, or
each other - so it was up to the party or player as to whom they
attacked.  The main problem however in a shared game was that the monster
had to move once only for each move - so I implemented this by allowing
the monster to move as fast as the fastest player.  This worked out
fairly well demanding coordination between players for their party
survival.  Network hack/rogue also allows for more magical items - e.g. a
scroll of cure blindness, which is useless to you but can cure another
player, or a potion of possession which could allow possession of another
player's character...

The aim of the game was poor enough, i.e. to collect a talisman, but
there was only one talisman and only the character that got it could exit
the game - this ensured a good final battle amongst the players that
survived (who obviously were very powerful).

